{"jsonapi":{"version":"1.1","meta":{"links":{"self":{"href":"http:\/\/jsonapi.org\/format\/1.1\/"}}}},"data":[{"type":"node--hs_event","id":"bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e","links":{"self":{"href":"https:\/\/mrc.stanford.edu\/jsonapi\/node\/hs_event\/bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e?resourceVersion=id%3A64626"},"working-copy":{"href":"https:\/\/mrc.stanford.edu\/jsonapi\/node\/hs_event\/bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e?resourceVersion=rel%3Aworking-copy"}},"attributes":{"status":true,"title":"Large time behaviour in Fisher-KPP type equations","changed":"2026-10-29T21:37:47+00:00","path":{"alias":"\/events\/large-time-behaviour-fisher-kpp-type-equations","pid":60376,"langcode":"en"},"body":{"value":"\u003Cp\u003EThe question addressed in this talk is the precise time asymptotic location of the level sets of the solutions of a class of partial differential equations that are usually referred to as \u0022of the Fisher-KPP type\u0022, the acronym standing for Kolmogorov, Petrovskii, Piskunov. These equations arise in biology, ecology or population genetics; but also in probability, in the theory of branching random walks.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe sharpest information has, for a long time, come from probabilistic analyses. The goal of the talk is to present an alternative point of view which opens the way to the understanding of new situations, such as, for instance, nonlocal models, or models in heterogeneous media.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou can learn more about Professor Jean-Michel Roquejoffre \u003Ca href=\u0022https:\/\/www.math.univ-toulouse.fr\/~roque\/\u0022\u003Eon his website\u003C\/a\u003E.\u003C\/p\u003E","format":"basic_html","processed":"\u003Cp\u003EThe question addressed in this talk is the precise time asymptotic location of the level sets of the solutions of a class of partial differential equations that are usually referred to as \u0022of the Fisher-KPP type\u0022, the acronym standing for Kolmogorov, Petrovskii, Piskunov. These equations arise in biology, ecology or population genetics; but also in probability, in the theory of branching random walks.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe sharpest information has, for a long time, come from probabilistic analyses. The goal of the talk is to present an alternative point of view which opens the way to the understanding of new situations, such as, for instance, nonlocal models, or models in heterogeneous media.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou can learn more about Professor Jean-Michel Roquejoffre \u003Ca href=\u0022https:\/\/www.math.univ-toulouse.fr\/~roque\/\u0022\u003Eon his website\u003C\/a\u003E.\u003C\/p\u003E","summary":""},"field_hs_event_admission":null,"field_hs_event_date":{"value":"2026-11-06T00:30:00+00:00","end_value":"2026-11-06T01:30:00+00:00","duration":60,"rrule":null,"rrule_index":null,"timezone":""},"field_hs_event_experience":null,"field_hs_event_instances":[],"field_hs_event_link":null,"field_hs_event_location":"380Y","field_hs_event_map_link":null,"field_hs_event_registration":null,"field_hs_event_sponsor":null,"field_hs_event_stream":null,"field_hs_event_stream_info":null},"relationships":{"field_hs_event_audience":{"data":[],"links":{"related":{"href":"https:\/\/mrc.stanford.edu\/jsonapi\/node\/hs_event\/bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e\/field_hs_event_audience?resourceVersion=id%3A64626"},"self":{"href":"https:\/\/mrc.stanford.edu\/jsonapi\/node\/hs_event\/bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e\/relationships\/field_hs_event_audience?resourceVersion=id%3A64626"}}},"field_hs_event_category":{"data":[],"links":{"related":{"href":"https:\/\/mrc.stanford.edu\/jsonapi\/node\/hs_event\/bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e\/field_hs_event_category?resourceVersion=id%3A64626"},"self":{"href":"https:\/\/mrc.stanford.edu\/jsonapi\/node\/hs_event\/bf9076b0-61de-431e-8d21-62a968e81a5e\/relationships\/field_hs_event_category?resourceVersion=id%3A64626"}}},"field_hs_event_series":{"data":[{"type":"node--hs_event_series","id":"0dba53da